From: Vera-Parity <vera-parity@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:40:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add a four-backend differential harness and cross-backend
 effect goldens.

run_four_backend_differential() runs one verified u16 stream on the real
OmniBinaryVm, Wasm, the host x86-64 ELF executed natively, and the Stage-1
ELF executed natively, and normalizes each to (exit, stdout bytes); i64/
trit -> 8 bytes LE, bytes-returning fns -> the buffer dump. Every backend
runs under catch_unwind so host panics are recorded, and native runs have a
timeout. `omnic backend-diff <file|src> [args]` compares any program
byte-for-byte; `omnic backend-diff --suite` grades OMNI_DIFF4_GOLDENS.

Goldens use hand-derived expectations: P1 byte readback (8796075198218 @x=7;
acceptance test for the IGET/ISET byte-storage fix, now passing on VM+Wasm
after d2d6c13) + buffer dumps, P2 Stage-1 DROP parity (1/2/3 drops), P3
IMOD x%0 and MIN%-1 after TCMP, P4 trit-op clamping, P5 BR_POS/BR_NEG on
non-trit i64, P6/P7 pack5 flow and two buffers, P9 VM iset_patch_i64
negative offset, P11 if_pos / while_sum_even / pack5 / decision_hook.

Confirmed bugs are listed in OMNI_DIFF4_KNOWN_DIVERGENCES with file:line;
strict xfail: a listed backend that starts passing fails with XPASS so the
fixing commit must remove its entry. No backend code is changed.
Selftest 13AY: 93 graded (58 pass, 35 xfail); 444 -> 537. Hashes unchanged.
